 "summary": {
  "headline": "Q1 FY27 revenue rose 14.3% YoY to INR51.4 crore, but adjusted EBITDA fell 14.5% to INR8.1 crore as growth investments were front-loaded into H1.",
  "overview": "Revenue grew 14.3% YoY to INR51.4 crore, with Uniware up 12.8% and Shipway up 16.8%. Adjusted EBITDA declined to INR8.1 crore from INR9.5 crore on planned investments in AI-led product, talent and sales and marketing. Reported PAT rose 20.2% to INR4.7 crore, helped by a tax benefit. Management expects Uniware and Shipway growth to reach 15%+ and 20%+ respectively from Q4 FY27, with profitability improving from H2 FY27.",
  "financial_highlights": [
   {
    "metric": "Revenue",
    "value": "INR51.4 crore",
    "change": "+14.3% YoY (from INR44.9 crore in Q1 FY26)"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Adjusted EBITDA",
    "value": "INR8.1 crore",
    "change": "-14.5% YoY (from INR9.5 crore)"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Adjusted EBITDA margin (calculated by analyst from figures above)",
    "value": "~15.8%",
    "change": "Not stated by management; cited by analyst Siva"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Reported EBITDA margin (as cited by analyst)",
    "value": "10.6%",
    "change": "Not stated by management"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Profit after tax",
    "value": "INR4.7 crore",
    "change": "+20.2% YoY (from INR3.9 crore); attributed to tax benefits recognised in the quarter"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Uniware standalone adjusted EBITDA",
    "value": "INR11 crore",
    "change": "Up from INR9.1 crore in Q1 FY26"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Cash and bank balances",
    "value": "INR92.6 crore",
    "change": "+72.1% YoY (from INR53.8 crore)"
   },
   {
    "metric": "ESOP expense",
    "value": "~INR2.5 crore in the quarter",
    "change": "Expected INR2.5-4 crore per quarter over the next year"
   }
  ],
  "segments": [
   {
    "name": "Uniware",
    "commentary": "Revenue up 12.8% YoY, the fourth consecutive quarter of improving growth; growth exceeded 15% excluding a former top-10 customer that exited in Q3 FY26. Added 115 enterprise customers (vs 88 a year earlier, +30.7%). Standalone adjusted EBITDA INR11 crore vs INR9.1 crore."
   },
   {
    "name": "Shipway",
    "commentary": "Revenue up 16.8% YoY, with 15%+ growth over the last two quarters. Investment stepped up in FY27 (sales and marketing, platform, AI workflows) after near-breakeven operation for part of FY26; management targets 20%+ growth from Q4 FY27 and breakeven by Q3 FY27."
   },
   {
    "name": "ConvertWay",
    "commentary": "Described as performing steadily, with product being enhanced for wider use cases and larger enterprises; no financial figures disclosed."
   }
  ],
  "guidance_outlook": [
   "Uniware growth of over 15% from Q4 FY27 onwards, on a like-for-like basis after the top-10 client exit; longer term aim of late teens and beyond 20%.",
   "Shipway growth of 20%+ from Q4 FY27 onwards; Shipway to operate below adjusted EBITDA breakeven in H1 FY27 and reach breakeven from Q3 FY27.",
   "Investments front-loaded in H1 FY27, with profitability improvement expected from H2 FY27; investment quantum described only as 'a few crores' and continuing through the current quarter.",
   "Uniware adjusted EBITDA margin expected to stay in a similar ballpark to last year's ~40% level (management said it moved from 32% to 35% on a run-rate basis).",
   "ESOP expense expected at INR2.5-4 crore per quarter over the next year.",
   "NRR expected to stay at 100%+ for FY27, though not disclosed quarterly."
  ],
